{"id":"2751a859d290ac09","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-prop-bernoulli-shift.md","title":"Bernoulli Shift","display":"prop-bernoulli-shift — Bernoulli Shift","type":"proposition","metadata":{"type":"proposition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-prop-bernoulli-shift","aliases":["58-prop-bernoulli-shift"],"display":"prop-bernoulli-shift — Bernoulli Shift","depends_on":["[[58-df-function]]","[[58-df-product-measure]]","[[58-df-shift]]","[[58-df-ergodic]]","[[58-df-zfc-measure9-kolmogorov-sinai-entropy]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"proposition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-prop-bernoulli-shift"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-prop-bernoulli-shift</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"prop-bernoulli-shift — Bernoulli Shift"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"18ad6e37d70b294d\" href=\"?note=18ad6e37d70b294d\" title=\"58-df-product-measure\">58-df-product-measure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8306a79d3c8e988a\" href=\"?note=8306a79d3c8e988a\" title=\"58-df-shift\">58-df-shift</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"11a66aa01f6e941d\" href=\"?note=11a66aa01f6e941d\" title=\"58-df-ergodic\">58-df-ergodic</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"8bad3810e4165411\" href=\"?note=8bad3810e4165411\" title=\"58-df-zfc-measure9-kolmogorov-sinai-entropy\">58-df-zfc-measure9-kolmogorov-sinai-entropy</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Explicit relation signatures used below: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ergodic}_S\\subseteq V^{4}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ergodic}_S\\subseteq V^{4}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S\\subseteq V^{6}\">\\(\\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S\\subseteq V^{6}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure9KolmogorovSinaiEntropy}_S\\subseteq V^{5}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure9KolmogorovSinaiEntropy}_S\\subseteq V^{5}\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\in V\">\\(A\\in V\\)</span> is a nonempty finite or countable alphabet and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Function}(\\alpha,A,[0,1])\">\\(\\operatorname{Function}(\\alpha,A,[0,1])\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sum_{a\\in A}\\alpha(a)=1\">\\(\\sum_{a\\in A}\\alpha(a)=1\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu_\\alpha\">\\(\\nu_\\alpha\\)</span> is the discrete probability measure on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(A,\\mathcal P(A))\">\\((A,\\mathcal P(A))\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu_\\alpha(\\{a\\})=\\alpha(a)\">\\(\\nu_\\alpha(\\{a\\})=\\alpha(a)\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,\\mathcal F,\\mu_\\bullet\">\\(X,\\mathcal F,\\mu_\\bullet\\)</span> are the constant <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb Z\">\\(\\mathbb Z\\)</span>-families with values <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,\\mathcal P(A),\\nu_\\alpha\">\\(A,\\mathcal P(A),\\nu_\\alpha\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S(\\mu_\\alpha,\\mu_\\bullet,X,\\mathcal F,\\Sigma_A,\\mathbb Z)\">\\(\\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S(\\mu_\\alpha,\\mu_\\bullet,X,\\mathcal F,\\Sigma_A,\\mathbb Z)\\)</span> is the product-measure predicate (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"18ad6e37d70b294d\" href=\"?note=18ad6e37d70b294d\" title=\"58-df-product-measure\">58-df-product-measure</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma_A\">\\(\\sigma_A\\)</span> is the two-sided shift graph defined in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"8306a79d3c8e988a\" href=\"?note=8306a79d3c8e988a\" title=\"58-df-shift\">58-df-shift</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ergodic}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Ergodic}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure9KolmogorovSinaiEntropy}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure9KolmogorovSinaiEntropy}_S\\)</span> are the predicates from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"11a66aa01f6e941d\" href=\"?note=11a66aa01f6e941d\" title=\"58-df-ergodic\">58-df-ergodic</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"8bad3810e4165411\" href=\"?note=8bad3810e4165411\" title=\"58-df-zfc-measure9-kolmogorov-sinai-entropy\">58-df-zfc-measure9-kolmogorov-sinai-entropy</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0\\log0\\coloneqq0\">\\(0\\log0\\coloneqq0\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}bernoulli\\text{-}shift}\\vdash{}&amp;\nA\\neq\\emptyset\\land|A|\\leq\\aleph_0\\land\n\\operatorname{Function}(\\alpha,A,[0,1])\\land\\sum_{a\\in A}\\alpha(a)=1\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\operatorname{Function}(X,\\mathbb Z,\\{A\\})\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(\\mathcal F,\\mathbb Z,\\{\\mathcal P(A)\\})\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(\\mu_\\bullet,\\mathbb Z,\\{\\nu_\\alpha\\})\n\\land\\forall a\\in A\\;\\nu_\\alpha(\\{a\\})=\\alpha(a)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S(\\mu_\\alpha,\\mu_\\bullet,X,\\mathcal F,\\Sigma_A,\\mathbb Z)\n\\land\\sigma_A=\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in(A^{\\mathbb Z})^2:\\forall i\\in\\mathbb Z\\;(y(i)=x(i+1))\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\mathrm{Ergodic}_S(\\sigma_A,\\mu_\\alpha,A^{\\mathbb Z},\\Sigma_A)\n\\land\\exists h\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure9KolmogorovSinaiEntropy}_S(h,\\sigma_A,A^{\\mathbb Z},\\Sigma_A,\\mu_\\alpha)\n\\land h=-\\sum_{a\\in A}\\alpha(a)\\log\\alpha(a)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}bernoulli\\text{-}shift}\\vdash{}&amp;\nA\\neq\\emptyset\\land|A|\\leq\\aleph_0\\land\n\\operatorname{Function}(\\alpha,A,[0,1])\\land\\sum_{a\\in A}\\alpha(a)=1\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\operatorname{Function}(X,\\mathbb Z,\\{A\\})\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(\\mathcal F,\\mathbb Z,\\{\\mathcal P(A)\\})\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(\\mu_\\bullet,\\mathbb Z,\\{\\nu_\\alpha\\})\n\\land\\forall a\\in A\\;\\nu_\\alpha(\\{a\\})=\\alpha(a)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S(\\mu_\\alpha,\\mu_\\bullet,X,\\mathcal F,\\Sigma_A,\\mathbb Z)\n\\land\\sigma_A=\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in(A^{\\mathbb Z})^2:\\forall i\\in\\mathbb Z\\;(y(i)=x(i+1))\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\mathrm{Ergodic}_S(\\sigma_A,\\mu_\\alpha,A^{\\mathbb Z},\\Sigma_A)\n\\land\\exists h\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure9KolmogorovSinaiEntropy}_S(h,\\sigma_A,A^{\\mathbb Z},\\Sigma_A,\\mu_\\alpha)\n\\land h=-\\sum_{a\\in A}\\alpha(a)\\log\\alpha(a)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The alphabet weights and all three constant <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb Z\">\\(\\mathbb Z\\)</span>-families are now registered set functions; pointwise equations alone did not fix their domains or functionality.</li>\n<li>Bernoulli shifts are the prototype of K-systems.</li>\n<li>Nontrivial Bernoulli shifts are K-systems and have completely positive entropy in the standard finite-entropy setting.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-product-measure","status":"resolved","id":"18ad6e37d70b294d","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-product-measure]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-shift","status":"resolved","id":"8306a79d3c8e988a","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-shift]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ergodic","status":"resolved","id":"11a66aa01f6e941d","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-ergodic]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-zfc-measure9-kolmogorov-sinai-entropy","status":"resolved","id":"8bad3810e4165411","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-zfc-measure9-kolmogorov-sinai-entropy]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-product-measure","status":"resolved","id":"18ad6e37d70b294d","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ProductMeasure}_S(\\mu_\\alpha,\\mu_\\bullet,X,\\mathcal F,\\Sigma_A,\\mathbb Z)$ is the product-measure predicate (see [[58-df-product-measure]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-shift","status":"resolved","id":"8306a79d3c8e988a","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\sigma_A$ is the two-sided shift graph defined in [[58-df-shift]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ergodic","status":"resolved","id":"11a66aa01f6e941d","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Ergodic}_S$ and $\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure9KolmogorovSinaiEntropy}_S$ are the predicates from [[58-df-ergodic]] and [[58-df-zfc-measure9-kolmogorov-sinai-entropy]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-zfc-measure9-kolmogorov-sinai-entropy","status":"resolv